{"agent":"fx-pins","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new regression assertion is too weak to prevent bug Ba17e75e10b from recurring. It adds `tests/data/uc_surf_knowledge_pin.json` to the set of files that must appear in *some* pin recipe, and separately asserts that *some* recipe is named `knowledge-pin`; it never verifies that the `knowledge-pin` recipe actually targets that file or that its `regen` command runs `tests/test_uc_surf_knowledge_pin.py` with `U1_PIN_RECORD=1`. A `pins.toml` containing a no-op `knowledge-pin` recipe whose `files` matches the JSON path would pass this test while still leaving the knowledge pin unregenerable. The test should load the `knowledge-pin` recipe and assert its regen command/env directly.","digest":"5d8784177688c1b1","location":"tests/test_pin_json_transcripts.py:25","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_pin_json_transcripts.py:25"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Previous issue #1 still holds for a no-op recipe. The new check only tests whether `\"tests/test_uc_surf_knowledge_pin.py\"` appears as a substring/element of `knowledge.regen`; it does not verify the command actually runs that script. A `.ddflow/pins.toml` knowledge-pin recipe whose loaded values are `files == (\"tests/data/uc_surf_knowledge_pin.json\",)`, `regen == \"echo tests/test_uc_surf_knowledge_pin.py\"`, and `env == {\"U1_PIN_RECORD\": \"1\"}` passes all three new assertions, but the pin is never regenerated, so the regression test still fails to prevent Ba17e75e10b from recurring.","digest":"f4595b0132d63e2c","location":"tests/test_pin_json_transcripts.py:30","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_pin_json_transcripts.py:30"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"e993e88f8cfcbef873dfa90c49d3dfe7ff0838cc","delta_raised":["f4595b0132d63e2c"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":935,"diff_sha":"5d30f7561a48c492b9e2f60859e69a4376267fc7531927208c33bef8875